put Cx 5 0
put Cx 1 sadd co32 38 1
o = cfeed cfr 16 cseq 0 get Cx 1 0 0
end
note Bytes past a FIN (review finding 9, RFC 9293 3.10.7.4). Data at offsets 5..15, a
note FIN at offset 5, then data 0..5: the FIN ends the stream at 5, so the 10 bytes stored
note beyond it are dropped (Tst 20), the application reads 5 bytes and the block is in
note CLOSE-WAIT acknowledging offset 6, also after the FIN is retransmitted. A FIN queued
note first cuts later data at its offset; a FIN at RCV.NXT drops what is stored beyond it.
