note RFC 6582 3.2 (review finding 5). The third duplicate ACK retransmits with ssthresh =
note max(FlightSize/2, 2 SMSS), recover = the highest sequence sent, cwnd = ssthresh + 3
note SMSS; each further duplicate ACK adds one SMSS, also after a partial ACK, up to
note 262144. A partial ACK retransmits the next hole and deflates cwnd by the bytes it
note acknowledges, adding one SMSS back only when they are at least one SMSS; the ACK of
note recover ends recovery at cwnd = ssthresh. A retransmission timeout ends recovery
note (ssthresh from the flight, cwnd one SMSS, recover = the highest sequence sent), and
note duplicate ACKs below recover then start no fast retransmit (recover starts at the
note ISS). A FIN that is the
note oldest unacknowledged octet is what a partial ACK retransmits.
